# ===========================================================================
# Profile (at-a-glance):
#   Model:     GLM-5.3-Flash (320.76B MoE, arch `glm5next`, unsloth UD-IQ4_XS —
#              146.1 GiB across 5 shards)
#   Engine:    llamacpp-club3090 v1.4 (fork: leloch's MoE expert cache v2 + our
#              L1/L3/E ports + vendored ggml-org/llama.cpp#27754 for `glm5next`)
#   Topology:  Dual 3090 PCIe (layer-split -ts 1,1, no NVLink)
#   Drafter:   ⛔ NONE — default SPEC_N=0. DFlash2 (the only drafter available)
#              DOES NOT LOAD on this engine, and block-45 MTP is unwired.
#              See Caveats. Toggle kept wired for when support lands.
#   KV:        fp16 (llama.cpp default — MLA keeps it compact)
#   Vision:    no (text-only here; no mmproj)
#   Max ctx:   204800 default — MEASURED + prefill-validated. 262144 also works;
#              204800 is chosen for CACHE HEADROOM, see Caveats
#   Genesis:   N/A — llama.cpp engine
#   Status:    🐣 Incubating
#   Best for:  long-context MoE serving experiments on the moe-cache engine
#   Caveats:
#     • ⚠️ ATTRIBUTION: the MoE expert cache is **leloch's** work
#       (github.com/leloch/llama.cpp, RFC ggml-org#24528). This slug packages
#       it; it does not originate it.
#     • ⛔ REQUIRES THE v1.4 ENGINE. `glm5next` arrives via vendored
#       ggml-org/llama.cpp#27754 (open draft, @danielhanchen). The v1.2 digest
#       shipped by the DeepSeek sibling CANNOT load these weights at all — this
#       is not a tuning difference, it is a hard architecture gap. Do not
#       repoint this image at a pre-v1.4 digest.
#     • ⚠️ #27754 vs #27752 — two rival PRs implement `glm5next` under the SAME
#       arch name. Unsloth's GGUF writes `glm5next.expert_shared_feed_forward_length`
#       and only #27754's converter emits it, so #27752 cannot read these
#       weights. If #27752 wins upstream, Unsloth re-converts and both the
#       vendored branch and the 146 GiB download become re-work.
#     • ✅ MAX CTX MEASURED 2026-08-28 by ladder — every rung booted AND served
#       a real prefill. Totals across both cards:
#         ctx      KV        compute     pool       slots  resid  prefill
#         32,768     528 MiB   7,682 MiB  27,296 MiB  7,126  ~19%  —
#        204,800   3,300 MiB  20,883 MiB  11,310 MiB  2,891   ~8%  68,286 tok ok
#        262,144   4,224 MiB  25,700 MiB   5,537 MiB  1,369   3.6% 87,401 tok ok
#       ⭐⭐ THERE IS NO HARD CONTEXT WALL HERE — THERE IS A CLIFF. VRAM sits at
#       22.6 GB/card at EVERY rung: it never nears OOM, because the expert pool
#       is elastic (free-minus-reserve) and simply absorbs whatever context
#       takes. Higher contexts keep BOOTING; what degrades is the cache.
#       ⚠️ So a boot-only test reports success right up until the pool hits zero
#       and CANNOT find the usable ceiling — only a decode bench can.
#       ⚠️⚠️ KV IS NOT THE BINDING CONSTRAINT — the COMPUTE BUFFER is. KV scales
#       linearly and stays small (MLA is compact); the compute buffer TRIPLED
#       (7,682 -> 25,700 MiB) and is what evicts the expert cache. Almost
#       certainly the DSA sparse indexer (indexer.top_k = 2048) sizing its
#       workspace against context.
#       ⇒ 262144 costs ~81% of the expert pool vs 32768; 204800 costs ~59%.
#       Quote that cost alongside any context claim; "262K works" alone is
#       misleading. The advertised 1,048,576 remains UNFITTED — do not quote it.
#       ⚠️ WHY 204800 AND NOT 262144 (the max that boots): at 262144 the cache
#       THRASHES. Measured 2026-08-28 at ctx=262144:
#         CUDA0 hits 17.6% used 504/504 evictions 65,323
#         CUDA1 hits 18.9% used 865/865 evictions 104,601
#       Every slot occupied with ~170k evictions = a working set that does not
#       fit, refilled over PCIe. Decode was 13.89 narrative / 13.67 code tok/s.
#       204800 doubles the pool (5,537 -> 11,310 MiB, 1,369 -> 2,891 slots), and
#       matches the DeepSeek sibling's context so their rows are comparable.
#       ⚠️ Hit rate tracked slot count almost exactly in the cross-model check
#       (GLM had 30% of DeepSeek's slots and 29% of its hit rate), which is why
#       slots — not MiB — is the number to reason about.
#     • ⛔⛔ THE DRAFTER DOES NOT LOAD ON THIS ENGINE — MEASURED 2026-08-28.
#       DEFAULT IS THEREFORE SPEC_N=0. rc2 implements DFlash1; the only
#       available drafter is DFlash2, and it fails at load:
#         `done_getting_tensors: wrong number of tensors; expected 81, got 58`
#       NOT a bad download (local size matches HF byte-for-byte; the GGUF header
#       itself says n_tensors=81). rc2 does not know 23 DFlash2 tensors: the
#       conv layers (attn_conv_base/proj + ffn_conv_base/proj, 4x5=20) and the
#       block-diffusion selector triple (selector_hidden/predecessor/successor).
#       81-23 = 58 exactly.
#       ⚠️ `--spec-type` CANNOT work around it: loading is driven by
#       `general.architecture` (= `dflash` in the file), not by the flag.
#       draft-dflash IS the right spec-type; the arch impl is incomplete.
#       ⚠️ It CRASH-LOOPS under `restart: unless-stopped` — the failure occurs
#       AFTER the 146 GiB target loads, so each retry costs ~3 min.
#       ⚠️ Licence: the DFlash2 GGUF is CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 (non-commercial,
#       no-derivatives), unlike the base model.
#       ⇒ GLM has NO working speculative path on this stack today (block-45 MTP
#       is unwired too). Set SPEC_N=5 only after the engine gains DFlash2
#       support. The -md/--spec-type flags below are left wired and INERT at
#       SPEC_N=0 (the entrypoint strips them) so re-enabling is one env var.
#     • ⚠️ DRAFTER LICENCE: the DFlash2 GGUF is **CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0**
#       (non-commercial, no-derivatives). Fine for this dev rig; check before
#       any downstream use or redistribution.
#     • ⚠️ `-devd ${DRAFT_DEVICE:-none}` DEFAULTS TO HOST, and the default is
#       inherited caution, NOT a GLM measurement. On the DeepSeek sibling a
#       GPU-resident drafter made the expert cache record **ZERO hits**
#       (device-list reorder in the shared-draft path). That drafter was
#       10.4 GiB; this one is 0.70 GB, so the CAPACITY half of that objection
#       does not apply — but the reorder half is size-independent. TEST IT:
#       boot with DRAFT_DEVICE=1 and read the moe-cache hit rate. Non-zero ⇒
#       GPU1 residency is a win (host drafters cost ~7-15% on the sibling).
#       Zero ⇒ revert to none. One env var between the two arms.
#     • ⚠️ moe-cache RESERVE_MB / ADMIT_AFTER below are INHERITED from the
#       DeepSeek sibling and are NOT measured on GLM. They were derived from a
#       compute-buffer swing measured on a DIFFERENT model. Re-derive before
#       quoting any tuned number for this slug.
#     • ⚠️ QUALITY UNTESTED. No 8-pack, no soak. Both the cache and the drafter
#       touch the generation path. Stays 🐣 until verify-full + bench + quality.
#     • ⚠️ COLD-START TAX: the first request after boot is slow while the expert
#       pool fills. Do not benchmark the first request.
#     • ⚠️ MODEL_DIR must point at the root CONTAINING `glm-5.3-flash-gguf`.
#       On this rig that is `/mnt/models/huggingface` — NOT `/opt/ai/models`,
#       where the DeepSeek sibling's weights live. The two roots differ.
#
#   Sampling (for bench/quality runs):
#     temperature 1.0 · top_p 0.95
#     ✅ VENDOR DEFAULT, confirmed 2026-08-28 from THREE sources: (1)
#     generation_config.json on zai-org/GLM-5.3 AND zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash,
#     (2) the GGUF's own general.sampling.temp / general.sampling.top_p,
#     (3) the card's HLE/BabyVision eval settings.
#     ⚠️ Do NOT quote the README's per-benchmark numbers as a default — they
#     vary (top_p=1.0 for NL2Repo/Terminal-Bench; temp=0.95 for DeepSWE).
#     ⚠️ bench.sh pins the STACK PROTOCOL sampler (temp 0.6/top_p 0.95/top_k 20)
#     for cross-engine comparability. Fine for TPS; QUALITY runs must use
#     temp 1.0 / top_p 0.95.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

services:
  llama-cpp-glm53-flash-iq4xs-moecache:
    # Digest-pinned, not tag-pinned: tags move, digests do not (#940 precedent).
    # v1.4-rc2, built 2026-08-28 from stack/club3090-moecachev1.4-models,
    # carrying vendored #27754. See the engine-gap caveat above.
    image: ${LLAMACPP_CLUB3090_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/noonghunna/llamacpp-club3090@sha256:bf2776f7db8e989749cf17cb03c62af08bffff15e324cccb4593b571071cb68f}
    container_name: ${ESTATE_CONTAINER:-llama-cpp-glm53-flash-iq4xs-moecache}
    restart: unless-stopped
    # Reap orphaned children. Without this a wedged llama-server becomes a
    # <defunct> PID 1 child holding GPU + host RAM.
    # ⚠️ NOT A CURE — measured 2026-08-28: a compose WITH `init: true` still
    # wedged 3× in one session ("did not receive an exit event") with an
    # unreaped <defunct> holding ~21 GB VRAM. Recovery is
    # `kill -9 $(docker inspect <c> --format '{{.State.Pid}}')`, not
    # `docker rm -f`. See LEARNINGS.md 2026-08-28.
    init: true
    ports:
      - "${BIND_HOST:-0.0.0.0}:${ESTATE_PORT:-${PORT:-8031}}:8080"
    volumes:
      - "${MODEL_DIR:-/mnt/models/huggingface}:/models:ro"
    environment:
      # Drafter toggle - docker forwards only what is declared here.
      - SPEC_N=${SPEC_N:-}
      - SPEC=${SPEC:-}
      # Expert-cache tuning — ⚠️ INHERITED from the DeepSeek sibling, NOT
      # measured on GLM. See Caveats.
      - GGML_CUDA_MOE_CACHE_ADMIT_AFTER=${MOE_ADMIT_AFTER:-64}
      - GGML_CUDA_MOE_CACHE_RESERVE_MB=${MOE_RESERVE_MB:-1536}
      # Cache hit/miss telemetry. Needs BOTH this AND LLAMA_ARG_LOG_VERBOSITY=4
      # — the moe-cache log line is GGML_LOG_INFO and the server's verbosity
      # threshold drops it below 4, so without `-lv 4` the whole cache subsystem
      # is silent and bench.sh renders the absence as a measured 0.0% hit rate.
      # DEFAULT 0 (OFF): telemetry is opt-in. Set MOE_STATS=200 for a bench run.
      - GGML_CUDA_MOE_CACHE_STATS=${MOE_STATS:-0}
      # Prefill expert-prefetch. PINNED OFF: it allocates a staging ring
      # (2 x 1088 MiB measured on the sibling) that competes with the expert
      # pool and with context headroom. Stack decision 2026-08-27.
      - GGML_EXPERT_PREFETCH=${EXPERT_PREFETCH:-0}
      # Bare passthrough — forwarded ONLY if the caller sets it. Never write
      # `=${VAR:-}`: docker would set it EMPTY, which is not the same as unset.
      - LLAMA_ARG_LOG_VERBOSITY
    deploy:
      resources:
        reservations:
          devices:
            - driver: nvidia
              device_ids: ['${ESTATE_GPUS:-0,1}']
              capabilities: [gpu]
    entrypoint:
      - /bin/bash
      - -c
      - |
        # -- Drafter toggle -------------------------------------------------
        #   SPEC_N=<n>  drafter depth; SPEC_N=0 disables
        #   SPEC=off    back-compat alias for SPEC_N=0
        # Disabling REMOVES the drafter flags rather than passing n=0: at
        # --spec-draft-n-max 0 llama.cpp sets drafting=false but still builds
        # the draft context and loads the draft model, so the memory stays
        # spent. A non-numeric SPEC_N is a hard error, so a typo can never
        # masquerade as a silent "drafter off".
        #
        # -- Threads --------------------------------------------------------
        # Default 28, NOT nproc/2. llama.cpp's own default collapses CPU-offload
        # decode, and on this 32c/8-channel host `-t 28` measured ~20% faster
        # than nproc/2=16. 28 is also the value GLM bring-up was validated at
        # (2026-08-27). ⚠️ This DIFFERS from the launcher's resolve_offload_threads
        # (nproc/2) — deliberate, and the reason it is pinned here explicitly.
        if [ -n "$${THREADS:-}" ]; then
          export LLAMA_ARG_THREADS="$${THREADS}"
          echo "[threads] -t $${LLAMA_ARG_THREADS} (THREADS set explicitly)" >&2
        else
          export LLAMA_ARG_THREADS=28
          echo "[threads] -t 28 (slug default; validated for GLM bring-up)" >&2
        fi

        _spec_n="$${SPEC_N:-0}"
        case "$${SPEC:-}" in off|OFF|Off|false|no|0) _spec_n=0 ;; esac
        case "$$_spec_n" in
          ""|*[!0-9]*)
            echo "[spec] SPEC_N='$$_spec_n' is not a non-negative integer." >&2
            echo "[spec] Fix: SPEC_N=<n> sets depth; SPEC_N=0 (or SPEC=off) disables." >&2
            exit 1 ;;
        esac

        if [ "$$_spec_n" -gt 0 ]; then
          # Fail loud if the external DFlash2 drafter GGUF is absent. The
          # model's OWN block-45 MTP head is not wired by #27754, so this
          # external drafter is the ONLY speculative path — a missing file
          # otherwise crash-loops on a cryptic gguf_init_from_file error.
          _draft=""; _want=0
          for _a in "$$@"; do
            if [ "$$_want" = 1 ]; then _draft="$$_a"; _want=0; continue; fi
            case "$$_a" in -md|--model-draft|--spec-draft-model) _want=1 ;; esac
          done
          if [ -n "$$_draft" ] && [ ! -f "$$_draft" ]; then
            echo "[spec] FATAL: external DFlash2 drafter not found:" >&2
            echo "[spec]   $$_draft" >&2
            echo "[spec] This slug REQUIRES it (block-45 MTP is unwired => no other spec path)." >&2
            echo "[spec] Fix one of:" >&2
            echo "[spec]   - download it: /opt/ai/hf-download.sh Anbeeld/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-GGUF \\" >&2
            echo "[spec]       <MODEL_DIR>/glm-5.3-flash-gguf/dflash2 GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-Q4_K_M.gguf" >&2
            echo "[spec]   - or run drafter-off knowingly: SPEC_N=0" >&2
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "[spec] drafter ON (SPEC_N=$$_spec_n)" >&2
          exec /app/llama-server "$$@"
        fi

        ARGS=(); _skip=0
        for _a in "$$@"; do
          if [ "$$_skip" = 1 ]; then _skip=0; continue; fi
          case "$$_a" in
            --spec-type|--spec-draft-model|--spec-draft-n-max|--spec-draft-n-min|-md|--model-draft|-devd|--spec-draft-device) _skip=1; continue ;;
          esac
          ARGS+=("$$_a")
        done
        echo "[spec] drafter OFF (SPEC_N=0 / SPEC=off) - drafter flags removed" >&2
        exec /app/llama-server "$${ARGS[@]}"
      - --
    # ⚠️ LIST FORM, NOT a folded `command: >-` string — REQUIRED, not style.
    # Compose's command-line parser REJECTS `(gate|up|down)` inside a folded
    # string. The list form skips shell parsing so the regex survives verbatim.
    command:
      - '-m'
      - '/models/glm-5.3-flash-gguf/UD-IQ4_XS/GLM-5.3-Flash-UD-IQ4_XS-00001-of-00005.gguf'
      - '--host'
      - '0.0.0.0'
      - '--port'
      - '8080'
      - '--alias'
      - 'glm-5.3-flash'
      - '-np'
      - '1'
      - '-c'
      - '${CTX:-204800}'
      - '-ngl'
      - '99'
      - '-sm'
      - 'layer'
      - '-ts'
      - '1,1'
      - '-fa'
      - 'on'
      # ⚠️ SINGLE -ot with comma-separated rules. Current mainline DEPRECATES
      # repeated -ot and honours ONLY THE LAST occurrence.
      # ✅ Stock regex is CORRECT for glm5next — verified 2026-08-27 against the
      # real tensor list: it matches the three routed expert tensors, and
      # correctly EXCLUDES `*_shexp` (the single shared expert, which fires every
      # token) and `ffn_gate_inp` (the router). Blocks 0-2 are dense
      # (leading_dense_block_count=3) and carry no `*_exps` tensors at all, so
      # they simply do not match — correct by construction, no special case.
      - '-ot'
      - 'blk\.[0-9]+\.ffn_(gate|up|down)_exps\.weight=CPU'
      - '-ub'
      - '${UBATCH:-4096}'
      - '-b'
      - '${UBATCH:-4096}'
      - '--cache-prompt'
      # --no-mmap: with -ot ...=CPU the offloaded experts must be resident, not
      # page-cache-backed. Validated for GLM 2026-08-28 (two runs, both correct
      # and terminating) — GLM is NOT affected by the --no-mmap defect that
      # blocks Qwen3.8-Flash-Next.
      - '--no-mmap'
      - '-md'
      - '/models/glm-5.3-flash-gguf/dflash2/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-Q4_K_M.gguf'
      # ✅ VERIFIED 2026-08-28 from the drafter GGUF's own metadata
      # (general.architecture = `dflash`): draft-dflash IS the right spec-type.
      # INERT at SPEC_N=0 — the entrypoint strips these flags. See Caveats for
      # why the drafter cannot load at all on this engine.
      - '--spec-type'
      - 'draft-dflash'
      - '--spec-draft-n-max'
      - '${SPEC_N:-0}'
      # Drafter device. Default host; DRAFT_DEVICE=1 puts it on GPU1. See Caveats
      # — this is the one knob worth A/B-ing first on this slug.
      - '-devd'
      - '${DRAFT_DEVICE:-none}'
      - '--moe-cache'
      - '${MOE_CACHE:-auto}'
      - '--fit'
      - 'off'
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -sf http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1"]
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 10s
      retries: 40
      # 146 GiB across 5 shards with --no-mmap; bring-up measured 4:03 to load.
      start_period: 900s
